<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How account, order and payment information is handled in Pashu Saathi."><div class="container"><header class="page-heading"><h1>Privacy</h1><p>Read this before signing in or sharing order details. Shop contact details and the final retention schedule must be confirmed before production launch.</p></header><article class="prose section"><h2>Information used to fulfill enquiries</h2><p>Google sign-in identifies your account. Your name, phone contact, delivery address, enquiries, quotes, orders, bills and payment evidence are used to process purchases and support account enquiries. Phone verification and staff confirmation are distinct; matching phone numbers do not automatically link accounts.</p><h2>Service providers and access</h2><p>Neon provides managed account, database, API and private file-storage services. Firebase and Brevo are optional notification providers; phone verification and notification delivery remain unavailable until their Neon integrations are configured and verified. Authorized shop staff can access information needed for shop operations. Never put payment details or passwords in public product enquiries.</p><h2>Optional browsing analytics</h2><p>When enabled by the shop, Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity require your permission on each eligible public catalog page. They are not loaded in the native apps, on account or admin pages, for signed-in customers, or on pages with search queries or fragments. Declining does not prevent browsing or ordering. Use “Keep analytics off” to withdraw permission on the current page.</p><p>The application sends a limited catalog page-view event to Google Analytics and masks rendered content before loading Clarity. These external providers may also process technical information such as your IP address and browser details. Provider settings and effective masking must be verified before collection is enabled. Private quotations, customer instructions and payment evidence must not be sent to browsing analytics.</p><h2>Error reporting</h2><p>When enabled by the shop, Sentry receives a generic application-render failure code and a random reference identifier. The application does not include exception messages, stack traces, page URLs, customer records, payment details or browsing breadcrumbs in that report. Direct reporting still exposes normal connection metadata, including your IP address, to the provider. Reporting is bounded and does not retry failed submissions; the recovery screen works even when reporting is disabled or unavailable.</p><h2>Storage on your device</h2><p>Your bag list stores public package identifiers and quantities. Offline storage holds public catalog pages and application code only, not account history, private payment attachments or ledger records. Sign-in sessions may be stored by the authentication client so you can remain signed in; use sign out on a shared device.</p><h2>Payments and notifications</h2><p>Payment screenshots are private evidence, not confirmation of payment. Staff must verify receipt. Notification permissions are optional and can be revoked in your device settings. SMS verification, where enabled, is optional and may be unavailable.</p><h2>Deletion and retention</h2><p>You can request deletion through your account. Necessary transaction and accounting records may need to be retained; the shop must explain the applicable scope and retention period when processing the request. No automatic deletion deadline is promised by this preview.</p><p><a href="/account-deletion/">How to request account deletion</a> · <a href="/contact/">Shop contact details</a></p></article></div></BaseLayout>
